[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Before attempting object interaction, verify that the target object exists, is visible/reachable, and is in the robot's current location; otherwise navigate to it or confirm visibility first. Before issuing a movement command, check that the intended path is clear. If an obstacle blocks the path, do not assume forward movement will succeed—replan, navigate around the obstruction, remove it if appropriate, or choose another route. Action predictions are unreliable unless preconditions are checked, so monitor the outcome of each action and adapt when something fails.

## Preliminary Thinking
1) Locate the green round fruit by exploring or checking likely surfaces; confirm it is present and reachable. 2) Navigate toward the fruit, checking the path for obstacles and replanning around any blockage. 3) Pick up the fruit, then verify the pickup succeeded (e.g., object is held/in inventory). 4) Locate the large gray furniture with a backrest (likely a sofa/couch or armchair). 5) Navigate to the furniture while checking that the route is clear; if blocked, replan or remove/move around the obstruction. 6) Place or move the fruit onto/at the target furniture and verify the delivery succeeded. If any step fails, diagnose the precondition (target not present/reachable, path blocked, wrong location) and retry with an adjusted plan.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]